<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- =====================================================================
     PRJEDU_opcua - AyMON example: an OPC UA client, against a machine
     that has its own OPC UA server.

     The machine is sim/ua_machine.py: a simulated injection moulding
     machine behind a real OPC UA server (asyncua, somebody else's stack),
     on opc.tcp://127.0.0.1:4840/moulding/. Start it first:
     run_machine.bat (needs setup.bat once - see the README).

     UA/S00 is the engine's side, with three connections to that machine:

       CN_UA   in the clear, Anonymous - what you have running in five
               minutes. It polls every second. The server lets an
               anonymous session read, and nothing else.
       CN_UAP  the same, for a subscription: the server sends a value
               when it changes. On a connection of its own, because a
               Publish waits at the server until there is news.
       CN_UAS  signed and encrypted (Basic256Sha256), logged in as the
               user 'setter' - what a plant should run. It writes the
               setpoint and the start/stop, and calls the machine's
               methods. It needs both certificates trusted: the machine's
               here (pro_trust), and ours on the machine (the README says
               how).

     The page: http://127.0.0.1:8102/

     Five connections, one document: inside the FREE edition.
     ===================================================================== -->
<xdb id="XDB" xdb_lib="AyPRO" xdb_log="4" log_cfg="0x39C0" log_lnk="%PRJ%/log/XDB.log"
     sta="0x0300" tid="S01">
	<config>
		<doc id="UA/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_UA.xml" desc="the machine, over OPC UA" />
	</config>
	<data>
	</data>
</xdb>
